window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-069", "name_zh": "心灵感应", "name_en": "telepathy", "tagline": "不用开口，你每时每刻都在跟周围的心互通念头——心灵感应不是特异功能，是语言的底", "explanation": "在赛斯这里，心灵感应不是一种少数人才有的超能力，而是所有人、乃至所有细胞与生俱来的天生功能。它属于「内在感官」，在意识之下持续不断地收发念头、意图与情感。赛斯给出一个很反直觉的说法：语言本身就是靠心灵感应才有意义的——没有这层看不见的直接沟通打底，声音和符号根本无法被理解。它运作的原理不是两座孤岛硬架桥，而是「同类相吸」：有相似或同情之处的人之间才连得上，靠的是彼此信念与情感的呼应。因此你发出的每一个念头都会传出去、影响身边的人，而你对实相的信念也决定了你收得到哪一类信息。赛斯进一步说，它没有空间距离的限制，醒时、梦里都活跃，死后的人格与出生前的胎儿主要就靠它沟通，甚至整个物质实相的凝聚协作也离不开它。他还强调，收到的念头从不被原样复制，接收者会加上自己的「创造扭曲」造出一个非常接近却并非同一的思想。", "definitions": [{"zh": "心灵感应沟通在意识之下持续发生，如果没有心灵感应和内在感官的协助，语言本身就毫无意义。隐藏的线索就是让语言容易理解的符号。我曾经说过，内在感官经验实相，因为它存在于伪装模式之下，虽然伪装模式本身当然就是这种实相的一部分。", "en": "Telepathic communications go on continually beneath consciousness, and without the aid of telepathy and without the aid of the inner senses, language itself would be meaningless. The hidden cues are the symbols that make language intelligible. I have said before that the inner senses experience reality as it exists beneath camouflage pattern, though of course camouflage pattern is in itself part of this reality.", "source": "Session 34"}, {"zh": "在这个层次上的心电感应，是内在能量或内部能量（inside energy）对它自己在物质场域之内的物质形体所做的无形、非实质沟通。这种初级的心电感应不是思想本身的沟通，而是意图、欲望和目的的沟通。所以它是内在能量对它本身还在形成的各个不同面向所做的沟通，可以说是一条肉眼不可见的道路或桥梁的开关。", "en": "Telepathy on this level is the intangible, nonmaterial communication of inner energy, or inside energy, to the physical materialization of itself within the physical field. This elementary telepathy is not the communication of thought as such, but is the communication of intent, desire and purpose. It is therefore the communication of inner energy to various still-forming aspects of itself, a blazing, so to speak, of invisible paths or bridges.", "source": "Session 121"}, {"zh": "心电感应的沟通无时无刻不在进行，而它之所以常在无意识的层次上发生，只因你的意识心是在一种“变位的状态”（State of becoming）,它没法留住你所拥有的全部资料。举个例子，如果你有意识的念头比较偏向“正面”，你就将会对同性质的心电感应资料起反应，纵使你只在无意识的层次上这样做。", "en": "Telepathic communication is constant. This is usually at an unconscious level merely because your conscious mind is in a state of becoming. It cannot hold all of the information you possess. As an example, if your conscious ideas are relatively positive you will react to telepathically received information of a similar nature, even if you do so on an unconscious level.", "source": "Session 617"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "心灵感应属于内在感官，语言靠它才有意义", "note": "赛斯说心灵感应是内在感官的一种，一直在意识之下运作。最反直觉的是：他不是说它除了语言之外另有一种沟通，而是说语言本身就建立在它之上——没有这层看不见的心灵感应打底，说出来的话根本无从被理解。你听一句话能懂，靠的不只是声音，还有一层直接接住对方意思的内在接收。", "src": "第 34、37、57、63、64、724、513 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 34 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 57 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 63 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 64 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 724 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 513 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0018", "zh": "心灵感应沟通在意识之下持续发生，如果没有心灵感应和内在感官的协助，语言本身就毫无意义。隐藏的线索就是让语言容易理解的符号。我曾经说过，内在感官经验实相，因为它存在于伪装模式之下，虽然伪装模式本身当然就是这种实相的一部分。", "en": "Telepathic communications go on continually beneath consciousness, and without the aid of telepathy and without the aid of the inner senses, language itself would be meaningless. The hidden cues are the symbols that make language intelligible. I have said before that the inner senses experience reality as it exists beneath camouflage pattern, though of course camouflage pattern is in itself part of this reality.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第34节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "34", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0021", "zh": "你们甚至不会用任何信任的态度使用外在感官来感知伪装实相。心电感应属于内在感官，它一直被使用着。没有了心电感应，你们的语言也将没有意义。菲利普，内在感官会即时经验直接资料。", "en": "You do not even perceive camouflage reality with your outer senses with any dependability. Telepathy, which belongs to the inner senses, is used constantly. Without it your languages would be meaningless. The inner senses, Philip, experience direct data instantaneously.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0033", "zh": "皮肤和骨骼是物质的，是足以束缚其他物质的界限，但是它们抓不住非物质的东西。一个人的意图会被他接触的人在潜意识上感觉到。口说的语言因心灵感应而有效用。没有心灵感应，语言就无法被理解。皮肤的外层，虽然是一道物质的围场，但就差别而言，只不过是为了方便才当作围场来用。", "en": "The skin and bone, being physical, are adequate barriers to bound other material, but they have no hold over what is not material. A man’s intent is subconsciously sensed by everyone with whom he comes in contact. Telepathy accounts for the usefulness of spoken language. Without telepathy no language would be intelligible. The outward layer of skin, while serving as a physical enclosure, serves as a physical enclosure only for the sake of convenience, as far as distinctions are concerned.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第57节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "57", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0034", "zh": "我告诉过你们，没有心电感应，语言就没有意义也没有效力。你们每一个人建构他自己的物质宇宙，并对它起反应，这是真的。透过连续不断的心电感应，你们才熟悉，其他人对他们近似的物质宇宙抱持的概念，这也是真的；而且当你建构并看见你自己的物质宇宙时，你建构任何一个物体，也都会透过心电感应，从其他人那里接收到它近似的大小、宽度、厚度和位置并列入考虑。", "en": "I told you that without telepathy language would be meaningless and ineffective. It is true that each of you constructs his own physical universe, and responds to it. It is also true however, that through continuous telepathy you are acquainted with the ideas of others concerning their approximate physical universes; and while you construct and see your own, you also construct any given material object taking into consideration its approximate size, width, thickness and location, as received through telepathy from others.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第63节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "63", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0035", "zh": "很显然，有许多需要解释的点，但这个事实绝对没有例外。心灵感应在建构的世界里是主要的黏着剂之一。你们可能称之为一个物体的东西，可能有几近无数的建构和相似度，相似度似乎这么大，只因为你们看到的是这么少。", "en": "There are, obviously, many points to be explained, but there are absolutely no exceptions to it. Telepathy is one of the main binders in the world of constructions. The similarities, and there may be an almost endless number of constructions of what you might call one physical object, the similarities only seem so great because you see so little.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第64节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "64", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0294", "zh": "可是，在这之下有基本的内在声音，所有的语言均建立其上。在于某些形象发出它们自己的声音，而两个在一起显示出清楚与精确的意义。许久以前我说过，语言要不是有心电感应的基础就会是不可能的——而沟通是由极微小的形象与声音结集起来的，这些然后被转译成不同的语言。", "en": "Underneath this, however, there are basic inner sounds upon which all language is based, in which certain images give forth their own sound, and the two together portray clear, precise meaning.2 A long time ago I said that language would be impossible were it not for its basis in telepathic communication3 — and that communication is built up of microscopic images and sounds. These are translated into different languages.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第723节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "723", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0247", "zh": "实际来说，我们在这些方面比你们进步得多，而当我们创造这些形相时我们是完全知道的。我与其他多少面对同样挑战，并有同样的全盘发展模式的“人”共享我的存在领域。这些“人”中有些我认识，有些则否。我们以心电感应沟通，但心电感应也同样是你们的语言的基础，没有心电感应的话，语言的象征符号将毫无意义。", "en": "Practically speaking, we are rather more advanced along these lines than you, and when we create such forms we do so with complete awareness. I share my field of existence with others who have more or less the same challenges to meet, the same overall pattern of development. Some I have known and others I have not. We communicate telepathically, but then again, telepathy is the basis for your languages, without which their symbolism would be meaningless.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第513节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "513", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "它一刻不停，只是你意识不到", "note": "赛斯反复强调，心灵感应是在潜意识层持续运行的，你依据收到的资料行动，可那个熟悉的有意识自我却毫不知情。它不挑地方、不挑时候：走路、坐着、听人说话时都在收发。你之所以觉得它稀罕，只是因为意识心这道闸门把大部分都挡在了觉察之下。", "src": "第 28、34、69、193、617 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 28 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 34 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 69 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 193 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 617 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0009", "zh": "而当这种心灵感应的能力发生时，持续执行这种心灵感应功能的是你这另一个自我意识的部分，但通常，你依据这类资料采取行动，但是你熟悉的那个有意识的自己却并不知道。今晚我至少要谈到这份资料，因为现在你听起来可能很复杂，但它真的是很基本。它是你们能够进一步之前一定要具备的知识。", "en": "When such abilities as telepathy occur, this telepathic function is carried on continually by this other self-conscious part of you, but as a rule you act upon such data without the knowledge of the conscious self with which you are familiar. I wanted to at least get into this material this evening, because while it may sound complex to you now, it is really basic. And it is knowledge that you must have before we can go further.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第28节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "28", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0205", "zh": "除了肢体和特定器官的残损外，没有（划线）任何的身体状况是不可逆的。用你们的话来说，人格始终都可以自由选择自己的未来。做这个选择的是内我，是真正的本体。当然，还有其他因素会影响这种情况，比如说，透过心电感应从别的地方得到暗示等。（停顿）", "en": "Now. No (underlined) physical condition is irreversible, with the exception of loss of limbs and definite organs. The personality is always free to choose, in your terms, its future. But the choice is with the inner self, which is the real identity. There are of course other elements entering into any such situation. Telepathically received suggestions from others, and so forth. (Pause.)", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第416节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "416", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0045", "zh": "心灵感应真的是和你们知道的空间距离无关。虽然如此，心灵感应代表的是一个影响范围。", "en": "It is true that telepathy has nothing to do with distance in space as you know it. Nevertheless, telepathy represents but one sphere of influence.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第69节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "69", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0111", "zh": "所有这些投射，皆有源自于该人格领域内的电磁实相与化学实相。能量的投射是你们族类的主要特征，个体在睡觉时会投射出梦和梦影像，醒时状态中也会，不过是在潜意识基础上投射的。 思想就是这样持续地放送出去，其他我们尚未讨论的投射也是如此。因此，一个个体怎么将这些投射放送出去，就怎么接收到来自其他人的投射。如你们所知，心电感应经常在自我的支配之下运作，于是形成你们的智性气氛（intellectual climate）。", "en": "All such projections have an electromagnetic and chemical reality that has its origin within the field of the given personality. This projection of energy is one of the main characteristics of your kind. Dreams and dream images are then projected by the individual in sleep, and also in the waking state, although on a subconscious basis. So are thoughts constantly sent outward, and other projections which we have not yet discussed. Therefore as the individual sends out these projections, so does he receive the projections of others. As you know, telepathy operates constantly beneath the dictates of the ego, and so is your intellectual climate formed.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第193节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "193", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0130", "zh": "心电感应的沟通是持续发生的……这发生在你们和鲁柏之间，当然也发生在和我之间。而约瑟以不同的方式了解事情；以非常常规的方式，因此他收到其他的东西……", "en": "There is constant telepathic communication... This operates with you both and Ruburt, and of course with me. And Joseph knows things in a different way; not as direct as a rule, though he picks up other things...", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第203节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "203", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0282", "zh": "心电感应的沟通无时无刻不在进行，而它之所以常在无意识的层次上发生，只因你的意识心是在一种“变位的状态”（State of becoming）,它没法留住你所拥有的全部资料。举个例子，如果你有意识的念头比较偏向“正面”，你就将会对同性质的心电感应资料起反应，纵使你只在无意识的层次上这样做。", "en": "Telepathic communication is constant. This is usually at an unconscious level merely because your conscious mind is in a state of becoming. It cannot hold all of the information you possess. As an example, if your conscious ideas are relatively positive you will react to telepathically received information of a similar nature, even if you do so on an unconscious level.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第617节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "617", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "不只人和人之间——连细胞都在用它通讯", "note": "这是赛斯最铺开的一层：心灵感应是所有细胞天生具备的能力，身体内部细胞之间就在用它传讯息。他说没有真正的封闭系统，所以感应一直在进行。他甚至说，将来生物学被逼到墙角时，不得不承认细胞天生有这种我们叫作心灵感应的能力，否则很多问题根本无解。", "src": "第 120、121、557、921 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 120 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 121 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 557 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 921 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": "身体内部那一层", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0071", "zh": "朝着这些方向的成功实验，看起来是支离破碎的事件，只因为它们拥有其存在，以及让它们的存在成为可能的背景，不为人所知或不被人认可。心电感应一直不断进行着，我亲爱的朋友们，在所有的现实场域之中。心电感应在身体之内的细胞之间进行着。心电感应之所以存在，是因为没有一个系统真的是封闭的系统。", "en": "Successful experiments along these lines appear as disconnected happenings merely because the context in which they have their existence, and which makes their existence possible, is not known or recognized. Telepathy goes on constantly, my dear friends, in all fields of actuality. Telepathy goes on within the body between the cells. Telepathy exists because no systems are truly closed systems.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第120节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "120", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0073", "zh": "在最简单的活体结构中，心电感应是沟通的必需品，尤其于内在能量够集中而形成任何一种更加复杂的模式或神经结构之前。甚至在这样的神经结构和物质纠葛被逐步形成时，心电感应都在运作，依然是个必需品，是物质结构之内的通讯系统，而且也依然在处理无法透过任何物质媒介传递的资料，因为就其本质而言，它无法被转译成物质形体。", "en": "In the most simple of living structures telepathy is a necessity for communication, particularly before the inside energy is concentrated sufficiently to form any sort of more complicated pattern or nerve structure. Even when such nerve structures and physical complications are evolved telepathy operates, still a necessity as a communications system within the physical structure, and still handling data which cannot be carried through any physical medium, simply because it is untranslatable by its nature into physical materialization.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": "细胞天生就会", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0072", "zh": "这个研究本身需要先引介其他现实场域的知识。生物学已经走了很多步，但它最终一定会涉及所有有机体背后的无形成分，也会不得不开创一个全新的领域，朝着基本有机心理学（organic psychology）的方向走。它将会被迫承认所有细胞天生具有的能力，就是我们可称之为心电感应的能力，因为要回答很多问题，除此之外不会有其他的解决方法。", "en": "This study alone would involve an introduction into a knowledge of other fields of actuality. Biology has made many strides, but it must finally be concerned with that intangible which is behind all organisms, and it will be forced to the initiation of an entirely new field, along the lines of basic organic psychology. It will be forced to recognize the innate ability of all cells for what we may call telepathy, for there will be no other solution in answering many questions.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0074", "zh": "这些要点全都极为重要。要理清心电感应这个词本身，还有很多要说，因为有很多类型，从我说的话当中你应该看得出来。这本身是一个复杂的主题，可是当我说完它的时候，你就会看到，心电感应是在所有细胞之内一种切身的天生能力。", "en": "These points are all extremely important. Much will be said yet to clarify the term telepathy itself, since there are many types, which you should be able to see from what I have said. This in itself is a complicated subject, and yet when I am finished it will be shown that telepathy is an intimate, innate ability within all cells.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0258", "zh": "它极需一个使它安定的因素。原先，身体意识由于和母亲在生理上与心电感应上有很深的认同，而得到滋养与支持。在细胞间的沟通远比你想象的要深沉。如果只考虑到身体意识，则其认同在出生前几乎是完全的。", "en": "It greatly needs a stabilizing factor. Previously the body consciousness has been enriched and supported by deep biological and telepathic identification with the mother. The communication of the living cells is far more profound than you imagine. The identification is almost complete before birth as far as body consciousness alone is concerned.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第557节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "557", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0314", "zh": "对你的梦的一个评论。如你所假设的，它是属于心电感应一类。在所有地球活生生的细胞之间，有一个细胞的沟通，就好像地球本身是一个巨大的身体一样。你自己的知识、欲望、目的及意图，将你调准到一些这种沟通，所以，你对乔•本巴洛（我们在顶峰路的邻居）的关心，将你调准到他当时的身体及情绪状态。", "en": "A comment about your dream. It was, as you supposed, of a telepathic nature. There is a cellular communication between or among all of earth’s living cells, as if the earth itself were one large physical body. Your own knowledge, desire, purpose and intent tuned you into some such communications, so your concern for Joe Bumbalo (our next-door neighbor on Pinnacle Road) tuned you into his physical and emotional state at that time.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "它到底怎么运作：靠的是同类相吸，不是两个孤立的心硬连", "note": "赛斯把心灵感应分成不同层次。最基本的一层不是思想的传递，而是内在能量对还在成形中的自己沟通意图、欲望和目的。而我们平常说的那种，是它比较 advanced 的变形。关键判读在这里：它主要发生在「同类相吸」的时候——两个有相似或同情之处的人之间才连得上；自我以为自己是个封闭孤岛、感应是两座孤岛之间架桥，这个画面是被自我的限制性定义带偏的。", "src": "第 121 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 121 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": "能量对成形中的自己沟通意图", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0075", "zh": "现在。在它最简单的层次上，而这根本不简单，但是在它最基本的层次上，你们所谓的心电感应以下面的方式运作。", "en": "Now. On its simplest level, and this is hardly simple, but on its most basic level, what you call telepathy operates in the following manner.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0076", "zh": "在这个层次上的心电感应，是内在能量或内部能量（inside energy）对它自己在物质场域之内的物质形体所做的无形、非实质沟通。这种初级的心电感应不是思想本身的沟通，而是意图、欲望和目的的沟通。所以它是内在能量对它本身还在形成的各个不同面向所做的沟通，可以说是一条肉眼不可见的道路或桥梁的开关。而且在同时间，这些无形道路的铺设具有内在架构的作用，未来的物质线路或结构将会建立在它之上。", "en": "Telepathy on this level is the intangible, nonmaterial communication of inner energy, or inside energy, to the physical materialization of itself within the physical field. This elementary telepathy is not the communication of thought as such, but is the communication of intent, desire and purpose. It is therefore the communication of inner energy to various still-forming aspects of itself, a blazing, so to speak, of invisible paths or bridges. And at the same time the laying down of these intangible paths serve as the inner framework over which or upon which future physical lines or structures will be laid.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0079", "zh": "和内在能量经由我先前解释过的过程形成更复杂的完形一样，内在能量接着继续和它在四周创造的物质沟通。当内在能量想要建构一个比较复杂的完形时，它就必须以心电感应透过它在自己四周收集而成的物质，沟通这个意图，先形成一个比较复杂的内在心电感应模式，然后可以用物质来装满它。心电感应的运作方式很难解释，因为任何个体的自我和内我各有不同的定义。对人类来说，心电感应看起来一定是在两个或比较完全分开的自己之间发生的一种心智或心灵的沟通。自我，你们看看，对自己有一个定义，对它自己的限制也有自己的看法。", "en": "As inner energy forms more complicated gestalts through the processes that I have earlier explained, then inner energy continues its communication with the physical matter that it creates about it. When inner energy desires to construct a more complicated gestalt, then it must telepathically communicate this intent and purpose through the matter which it collects about itself, forming a more complicated inner telepathic pattern first, that can then be filled in with physical matter. The manners in which telepathy operates are difficult to explain because of the divergence of definition held by the ego and by the inner self of any given individual. To the human being it must appear that telepathy is a mental or psychic communication occurring between two or more entirely separate selves. The ego, you see, has one definition for the self and its own idea of the limitations of itself.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": "感应靠的是相似与同情", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0080", "zh": "自我自认为是这个自己，认为它的自己以外的任何东西，不是非自己，就是另一个分开的本体，所以一个人就被引导去相信，心电感应基本上是两个，或基本上比较单独、分开又远离的自己之间的沟通。心电感应不在自我的层次上运作，但是它的行动可能伸入自我的领土。心电感应在内我之内，在各个不同的层次、在潜意识各层之内运作，自己的分离和限制这些概念根本没有这么局限。", "en": "The ego considers itself the self and considers anything outside of its self as being either no self or another such separate identity, and so the individual man is led to believe that telepathy is basically a communication between two or more basically alone, separate and aloof selves. Telepathy does not operate at the level of the ego, although its actions may protrude into the domain of the ego. Telepathy operates within the inner self, within various levels, different levels of the subconscious, where the ideas of separation and limitations of self are not nearly so limiting.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0082", "zh": "每当内我向外联系时，不管是它的同情心或生命力被吸引，内在的心电感应沟通就存在。用我们以后会讨论的方式，在心灵上它包围资讯，以几乎和一个简单的阿米巴虫（amoeba）在身体上包围食物那样的方式，在心灵上运作。", "en": "Inner telepathic communications exist whenever the inner self reaches out, wherever its sympathies or vitalities are attracted. In a manner we will later discuss, psychically it surrounds information, operating psychically almost in the same manner that a simple amoeba physically will surround food.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0083", "zh": "这可能不是一个非常恰当的比喻，但无损于这个比喻背后的原理。这解释起来很复杂，但又急需解释，因为心电感应主要是在类似和吸引建立的时候，在同类相吸的时候运作；而不是像表面那样，在一个外来或分开的本体和另一个连结在一起的时候。", "en": "This may not be a very apt analogy, but the principles are sound behind the analogy. This is complicated to explain, and yet an explanation is sorely needed, for telepathy operates mainly when similarities and attractions are set up, when like attracts like; and not, as it would seem, when as it appears one alien or separate identity is connected with another.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0084", "zh": "我这里试着让你们明白的是，因为目前为止所做的表面研究，看起来心电感应似乎是在分离中运作，这是由于自我在对自己的定义上设定的限制所致。让心电感应成为可能的，是那些在心电感应沟通中的类似或同情。自我对自己的限制性概念，遮蔽和扭曲了主要的议题，因为自我对于同情之下隐含的连结没有意识，但那些连结却具有暂时融合相关本体的作用。", "en": "What I am trying to get across here is that, because of the superficial studies done so far, it seems that telepathy operates with separateness because of the limitations set by the ego on the definition of self. It is the similarity, or sympathy, of those in telepathic communication that makes telepathy possible. The limited idea of the self held by the ego clouds and distorts the main issue, for the ego is not conscious of the underlying bonds of sympathy that serve to merge, momentarily, the identities involved.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "你收不到原封不动的那个念头，也瞒不住自己", "note": "既然靠心灵感应相通，就有两件事要认。第一，传过去的念头从不会是原样：接收者会加上自己的「创造扭曲」，造出一个非常接近却并非同一的思想。第二，反过来，你的心思对身边人（甚至你眼中的敌人）其实大体是透明的，只是你不知道。赛斯说，若你对本体的性质看得更清，就不会害怕心灵感应——那份怕，底下其实是担心自己会被别人的念头卷走。", "src": "第 153、518、550 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 153 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 518 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 550 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": "收到的念头总被改写", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0086", "zh": "原本A所持有的这个思想，依然由A保留着，可是一个表面看似一模一样的思想却传到B。A什么都没有失去。也就是说，在送出这个思想时，在试着复制这个思想时，他自己还是保有它，所以传给接收者B的是什么，这很重要，因为一个解释对于说明发生在心电感应沟通常见的落差，很有帮助。", "en": "The thought originally held by A is still retained by A, yet a seemingly identical thought reaches B. A has lost nothing. That is, in sending the thought, in trying to duplicate the thought, he himself still retains it, so what is passed on to receiver B? This is rather important, since an explanation will do much to account for the frequent difference that occurs in telepathic communications.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第136节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "136", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0090", "zh": "就创造扭曲与行动的关系而言，创造扭曲会影响思想的创造。从一个个体传递到另一个个体的思想之所以不可能一模一样，主要原因就是创造扭曲的原理。这里应该思索一下我给你们的心灵感应资料。", "en": "Creative distortion, in its relationship with action, affects therefore the creation of thoughts. The principle of creative distortions is mainly responsible for the fact that no identical thought is ever transmitted from one individual to another. Here the material that I have given you on telepathy should be considered.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0091", "zh": "因此，在心电感应通讯中接收到的思想，不会是原本传输的思想，而是一个非常接近的思想，其实是接收者创造出来的一个创造扭曲。我提过的，本体无法复制。", "en": "The thought received in telepathic communications will not, therefore, be the exact thought that was transmitted, but a close approximation, a creative distortion, actually created by the receiver. There are, as I mentioned, no duplication of identities.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": "你其实藏不住", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0249", "zh": "因为我们用心电感应，所以纵使是我们想要彼此隐瞒，也是很难的。我相信，你们一定觉得这似乎侵犯了隐私权，但我向你保证，即使是在现在，你们的思想也是一无隐敝的，你的家人与朋友对它们都十分清楚，我再加一句，而且很不幸的，你的敌人对它们也一样清楚。你们只是不知道这事实而已。", "en": "Because we use telepathy we can hide little from each other, even if we wished to. This, I am sure, seems an invasion of privacy to you, and yet I assure you that even now none of your thoughts are hidden, but are known quite clearly to your family and friends — and I may add, unfortunately, to those you consider enemies as well. You are simply not aware of this fact.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第518节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "518", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0260", "zh": "的确是的。不过，心电感应真的存在。那么别人对你的所思所感大部分也都有所知觉。", "en": "It is, indeed. However, telepathy does exist. Others are aware, then, to a large extent of what you are thinking and feeling.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第558节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "558", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0250", "zh": "灵魂并不为它的身份感到害怕。它对它自己有信心。它总在探索。它不怕被经验或感知所淹没。如果你对本体的性质有更透彻的了解，你就不会，譬如说，害怕心电感应，因为在这种担心的背后你恐惧的是本体会被别人的暗示或思想卷走。", "en": "The soul is not frightened for its identity. It is sure of itself. It ever seeks. It is not afraid of being overwhelmed by experience or perception. If you had a more thorough understanding of the nature of identity you would not, for example, fear telepathy, for behind this concern is the worry that your identity will be swept away by the suggestions or thoughts of others.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第528节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "528", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "跟千里眼、预知，其实是一回事", "note": "赛斯干脆说，预知和心灵感应之间基本没有区别，看似不同只是因为不了解时间的本质；两者的共同点是——信息都不是从公认的感官进来的。他还提醒，千里眼管的是伪装图像，心灵感应管的是心与心之间不隔距离的念头与情感，现实里常常分不清到底用了哪一种，或者两种一起用。", "src": "第 29、66、240、242 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 29 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 66 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 240 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 242 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0011", "zh": "梦的资料就本质来说是正确的。你的朋友，卡拉汉小姐，说她就要走了，还说，她其实不想离开。梦中的画面，一部分是潜意识的猜测，其中还带有一点千里眼的意味。不管是利用心灵感应沟通或透过千里眼来接收讯息，这样的内在通讯基本是一样的，因为都是内在感官在接收。比如说，会看到什么地方，而不是听到什么话，是由讯息的接收者决定。", "en": "The dream data was correct in its bare essentials. Your friend, Miss Callahan, said that she was going away, and that she did not really want to go away. The picture in the dream was partly subconscious guesswork with a touch of clairvoyance. Any such inner communications are basically the same in that they are picked up by the inner senses, whether or not the information is received as a telepathic communication or in terms of clairvoyance. Where a place for example is seen, rather than words being heard, is determined by the receiver of the message.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第29节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "29", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0023", "zh": "鲁柏那张纸的经验代表一次千里眼，就像他的时钟经验一样；千里眼与伪装模式有关。比方说心灵感应就不是。在更进一步的这类经验中，随着能力的增强，鲁柏将能“看到”（引号）更多。", "en": "Ruburt’s experience with the slip of paper represented a clairvoyance, as did his experience with the clock; and clairvoyance is concerned with camouflage pattern. Telepathy for example is not. In further experiences of this kind, Ruburt will be able to “see” （in quotes） more as his ability grows.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0156", "zh": "基本上，预知和心灵感应之间没有任何区别。明显的差异是对时间本质了解不足造成的结果。重要的事实是，在这两种情况下，一个个体接收到的讯息并非来自公认的感官系统。", "en": "Basically there is no difference between precognition and telepathy. The apparent difference is the result of an inadequate understanding of the nature of time. The important fact is, in both cases, that information is received by an individual that does not come through recognized sense systems.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第240节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "240", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0246", "zh": "所有必要的资料都经由这些内在的通道给了你，即使在你能举一举指头或眨眨眼或读这一句话之前，不可置信的内在活动已经发生了。你本体的这个部分本自具足千里眼与心电感应的能力，因而在灾难发生前你已得到警告，不论你是否有意识地接受这信息。在一个字都还没有说之前，所有的沟通都早已发生了。", "en": "All necessary information is given to you through these inner channels, and unbelievable inner activities take place before you can so much as lift a finger, flicker an eyelid, or read this sentence upon the page. This portion of your identity is quite natively clairvoyant and telepathic, so that you are warned of disasters before they occur, whether or not you consciously accept the message, and all communication takes place long before a word is spoken.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0177", "zh": "有一些事情我不相信你清楚明了。对我来说，一个思想就是一个行动。它是一样有效的实相。按照你们用的词语，心电感应和千里眼之间没有任何基本的差异。与一个物品相连的情绪感觉，对我来说，与这个物品本身一样真实。被解读的是这些情感电荷，最后再翻译成实质的说法。", "en": "There are some things that I do not believe you clearly understand. To me, a thought is an action. It is as valid a reality. There is no basic difference between telepathy and clairvoyance, as you term them. The Emotional feelings connected with an item are as real to me as the item itself. It is these Emotional charges that are interpreted, and finally translated into physical terms.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第286节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "286", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0178", "zh": "好。如果有一个特定的问题被提出来，我们就会尝试回答它。答案当然是以同样的方式被接收，透过情感力量。前天晚上，你在心里回答了你自己的问题，于是我们接收到那个地点。不过，称之为心电感应并没有让你了解什么，因为这样的资讯全部都是情感力量的结果。", "en": "Now. If a particular question is asked, we attempt to answer it. The answer of course will be picked up in the same manner, through Emotional force. The other evening, you answered your own question in your mind, and we picked up that location. To call this telepathy tells you nothing however, for all such information is the result of Emotional force.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第286节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "286", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "你的念头会传出去，别人真的会被你影响", "note": "这块最实用。赛斯说心灵感应在潜意识层不断放送：你反复预期某人会怎样，就等于一直在朝他发那个方向的暗示，而每个人都会对暗示起反应。反过来，你停一停、温柔地改口想「他会好起来的」，就已经在帮他了。信念尤其如此——限制的念头会把同类念头吸过来，你也只会对与自己已有信念对得上的感应信息起反应。", "src": "第 329、340、616、619 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 329 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 340 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 616 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 619 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": "你的预期变成发给别人的暗示", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0191", "zh": "比方说，你必须在心智里消除负面意象。如果你认为明天强尼会在自习室捣乱，你就应该在你的心智里，用强尼表现良好的意象来代替它。首先，如果你想像某个学生会捣乱，你就会自动向他发送心电感应的讯息。如果他非常容易受暗示影响，那他就会落实你给出的暗示。", "en": "You must mentally wipe out the negative image, for example. If you think that tomorrow Johnny F will misbehave in study hall, you should, in your mind, replace this with the image of Johnny F behaving very well. In the first place, if you imagine that a particular student will misbehave, you are automatically sending him a telepathic message to that effect. If he is highly susceptible to suggestion, he will carry out the suggestions that you have given.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第332节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "332", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0192", "zh": "听好：你必须明白一件事，心电感应会在潜意识层面不断运作。如果你不断期望某人以某种方式行事，那么你就会经常向他发送这样做的心电感应暗示，每个人都会对暗示做出反应。接着，根据当时的具体情况，对方会在某种程度上按照自己收到的群体暗示（mass suggestions）而采取行动。", "en": "Now: you must understand, for one thing, that telepathy operates constantly at a subconscious level. If you continually expect any individual to behave in a particular manner, then you are constantly sending him telepathic suggestions that he will do so. Every individual reacts to suggestion. According then to the specific conditions existing at the time, such an individual will to some extent or another act according the mass suggestions he has received.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第340节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "340", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0193", "zh": "这些群体暗示，不仅包括其他人给他的口头和心电感应暗示，也包括他醒时或梦中给自己的那些暗示。如果某甲处于失望期，那是因为他已经成为自己和其他人负面暗示的牺牲品。假设你现在看到他，心想他看起来很悲惨——或者他是个无可救药的酒鬼——那么你虽然什么话都没说，但他潜意识确实会收到这些暗示，在这种精神脆弱的情况下，他就会接受这些暗示并付诸行动。", "en": "These mass suggestions include not only those given to him by others, both verbally and telepathically, but also those suggestions that he has given to himself while in the waking or dream states. If individual A is in a period of despondency, then this is because he has already become prey to negative suggestions of his own and others. If now you see him and think that he looks miserable—or that he is an incurable drunk—then indeed these suggestions are picked up by him subconsciously though you have not spoken a word, and in his already weakened condition, they will be accepted and acted upon.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第340节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "340", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0194", "zh": "反过来说，如果在相同的状态下你想到他，但是你停下来，温柔地对自己说：他现在开始觉得好一点了——或是他只是一时酗酒——这时的确会燃起希望，而你也已协助了他，因为这些暗示在心电感应层面上，至少代表少量的弹药，帮助他击退沮丧绝望。", "en": "If, on the other hand, thinking of him under the same conditions, you stop yourself and say gently to yourself : he will begin to feel better now—or his drinking is temporary—and there is indeed hope here, then you have given him aid, for the suggestions will at least represent some small telepathic ammunition to fight off the war of despondency.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第340节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "340", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0195", "zh": "这将是一节相对简短的课，我们很快就会结束。我要在此重复刚才的建议，请我们的朋友读一读我之前的资料。很重要的是，你们都必须了解你的态度和情感如何透过心电感应的运作影响别人，也要了解你最细微的起心动念如何影响自己的情绪和你意象的具体状况。", "en": "Now. This will be a relatively brief session and we shall end shortly. I will here repeat my earlier suggestion that our friend read my earlier material. It is important that you all realize the ways in which your attitudes and feelings affect others through telepathic workings, and the ways in which the smallest thought affects your own Emotions, and the physical condition of your image.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第340节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "340", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0231", "zh": "现成的答案无论给他还是给他儿子，都只会害了他们。他们会把它们当作借口。现在给我一点时间……我要告诉他：他对这个男孩的许多担忧，都是他自己恐惧的投射，并不会物质化。这个男孩正在以心电感应回应父亲的担忧，这只是其中一件事。父亲眼下能做的最好的事，就是单纯地善待这个男孩，同时在心里替孩子卸下那强压在他身上的思绪。让孩子一个人待着。他正在以心电感应接收父亲的负面态度。", "en": "Ready answers for he or his son would only betray them. They would use them as excuses. Now give me, a moment... I will tell him that many of his worries concerning the boy are projections of his own fears, and will not materialize. The boy is reacting telepathically for one thing to the father’s worries. The best thing the father can do for now is to be simply kind to the boy, but relieve the child of his heavy-handed thoughts mentally. Leave the boy alone. He is picking up the father's negative attitudes telepathically.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第472节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "472", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": "信念同类相聚、按已有信念挑着收", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0278", "zh": "你是心电感应的发讯者，也是个收讯人。因为意念有个电磁实相，而信念，因为它们的强度，发出强烈的辐射。由于你自己心理本质的组织结构，使得相似的信念集结到一块儿，而你会心甘情愿地接受那些你本已同意的信念。", "en": "You are a sender and a receiver. Because ideas have an electromagnetic reality, beliefs, because of their intensity, radiate strongly. Due to the organizing structure of your own psychological nature, similar beliefs congregate, and you will readily accept those with which you already agree.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0279", "zh": "因此，限制性的意念自动就会令你去接受那些类似的观念。同样的，那些洋溢着自由、愉悦与自发性的意念，也自动地把同类的想法吸了过去。人与人之间有着无休止的相互作用，其中充满了各种念头的交换，包括了意识上与心电感应上的。", "en": "Limiting ideas therefore predispose you to accept others of a similar nature. Exuberant ideas of freedom, spontaneity and joy automatically collect others of their kind also. There is a constant interplay between yourself and others in the exchange of ideas, both telepathically and on a conscious level.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0280", "zh": "再次，这种交换是根据你有意识的信念而进行。在某些圈子里流行着一种说法，他们相信不管你有意识的信念或意念为何，你都会对心电感应收到的讯息产生具体的反应。事实并非如此。（强调地）你只会对那些与你有意识的意念相合的心电感应讯息起反应，它们与你对自己及对实相的看法相契合。", "en": "This interchange follows, again, your conscious beliefs. It is fashionable in some circles to believe that you react physically to telepathically received messages despite your conscious beliefs or ideas. This is not the case. You react only to those telepathic messages that fit in with your conscious ideas about yourself and your reality (emphatically).", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "别把它供起来，也别怕它——它是意识的自然成分", "note": "赛斯的态度很平：心灵感应、千里眼这些不是人类经验里古怪孤立的例外，而是日常行为的自然模式，只是被官方那套实相画面盖住了。它也一直在你不知情的情况下帮你接收环境里他人的状态，就像你出于关心而自然调到对方的身心状况上。", "src": "第 246、469、484、771 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 246 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 469 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 484 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 771 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0229", "zh": "不言而喻，心电感应既是形成事件的方法，也是感知事件的方法；只是心电感应藏在物质感知极深的下方，几乎察觉不到。", "en": "It goes without saying that telepathy is one method by which events are formed as well as perceived, but telepathy hides so far beneath physical perception that it is hardly detected.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第469节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "469", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0236", "zh": "于是在目前的境况下，人满为患的情形还将进一步加速，直到一种新的综合形成——而它必定会形成。所引发的心灵活动终将奠定更深的相互理解的基础。到时候将十分明显：心灵感应的念头，传得比好消息更快、比瘟疫更迅疾。人类会被挤得如此紧密，以致那股冲撞将实实在在地爆发为一个新层面的意识，一次就这些条件而论的新发展。", "en": "And so in the present circumstance the overcrowded conditions will still be further accelerated, until a new synthesis is formed—and it will be. The psychic activity engendered will finally form the basis for a greater understanding. It will be quite obvious that telepathic thoughts travel quicker than good news or faster than a pestilence. Man will be so shoved together that the impact will literally explode into a new level of consciousness, a new development in those terms.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第484节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "484", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0310", "zh": "科学委派自然世界为自然事件的领域。所以，它对自然的观点是机械性的。可是，自然本身，像自然的其余部分一样，却都拥有一个丰富的内在心理上的深度，那是科学由于它自己的定义，所无法感知的。举例来说，心电感应和眼通，是自然效应的一部分，但它们却属于一个比科学定义广大得多的自然，以至于令它们看起来是非常不自然的古怪行为，而非意识的自然成分。", "en": "Science delegates the world of nature as the realm of exterior natural events. Its view of nature is therefore mechanistic. The natural self, however, like the rest of nature, possesses a rich dimension of inside psychological depth, that science, because of its own definitions, cannot perceive. Telepathy and clairvoyance, for example, are a part of natural effects, but they belong to a nature so much more expansive than science’s definitions that they have been made to appear as highly unnatural eccentricities of behavior, rather than as natural components of consciousness.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第4节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "4", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0311", "zh": "且说，自然人并不能在过去或现在找到，却是在一层又一层的官方信念底下，所以，要找到最开始创造信念的人，你是在处理信念的考古学。如我常说的，眼通、心电感应或不论什么的证据，并非发生在人类经验里的古怪而孤立的例子，却代表了日常行为的自然模式，那是由于行为和实相的官方画面而在你们世界里变得隐而不显的。", "en": "The natural person is to be found, now, not in the past or in the present, but beneath layers and layers of official beliefs, so you are dealing with an archeology of beliefs to find the person who creates beliefs to begin with. As I have said often, evidence of clairvoyance, telepathy, or whatever, are not eccentric, isolated instances occurring in man’s experience, but are representative of natural patterns of everyday behavior that become invisible in your world because of the official picture of behavior and reality.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第10节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0302", "zh": "等我们一会儿…… 如人类一向的发展，人类的幸存是与信念有关的一件事，这是远超过一般所了解的——因为某些信念现在已是与生俱来的了。他们变成与生物性相关而传送下去。在此，我指的并不是如心电感应式的传送，却是将信念转译成肉体的密码，而后变成生物上的指示。结果是，以生物性来说，一个男孩较易以某一种既定的态度行动。", "en": "(Pause at 9:35.) Give us a moment … Survival of the human species, as it has developed, is a matter of belief far more than is understood — for certain beliefs are now built in. They become biologically pertinent and transmitted. I mean something else here besides, for example, a telepathic transmission: the translation of beliefs into physical codes that then become biological cues. [As a result], it then becomes easier for a boy to act in a given manner biologically than in another.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第771节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "771", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0169", "zh": "当时他们并没有尝试做任何实验，但是他们的能量是自由的，并向外伸展。往往，在你没有发觉的时候，可以说你正在试用你的心灵翅膀。这相当重要。 你所谓的灵体多半都是在你不是有意识地做实验时去旅行。透过心电感应，你在没有试图接收它们的时候，接收到想法。然而，这并不是说有意识的实验没有用。而只是说，你有意识地设法在做的事情，你在一无所知的情况下一直都在做。", "en": "They were not trying any experiments at the time, but their energies were free, and reaching outward. Often you are trying your psychic wings, so to speak, when you do not realize it. This is rather important. What you call the astral body does much of its traveling when you are not consciously trying to experiment. Telepathically you receive thoughts when you are not trying to receive them. This does not mean that conscious experimentation will not work however. It simply means that what you are trying to do. consciously. you have been doing without knowing it all the while.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第246节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "246", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "梦里、死后、以及还没出生的时候，它都在", "note": "赛斯说梦里的感应比醒时还活跃：睡着时自我的屏障松开，感应和预知更自由地流动，一个梦者的梦会以感应传给另一个梦者。死后的人格主要就靠感应沟通，不用字词。甚至怀里的胎儿，在听见父母说话之前就先用心电感应相通，出生前的关系也靠感应来谈定。", "src": "第 193、195、202、242、535、541 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 193 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 195 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 202 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 242 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 535 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 541 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": "梦里最自由", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0114", "zh": "如我之前所说，有一个化学上的必然性，让做梦变成无可避免。不过一般而言，这些梦接着会反过来全面影响人格，也影响该人格在物质宇宙之内的行动。心电感应在梦境里运作的效果，跟在个体醒时运作的效果完全一样，这一点不必多说。在醒时状态下，心电感应在潜意识层面上运作。但一般来说，始终不会有任何的界限，能将一个心理个体与另一个心理个体分隔开来。不同的心理个体之间会有差异，你们就将注意力专注在这些差异上面。然而一个人的梦会影响到另一个人的梦，他旁边人的梦反过来也会影响到他。", "en": "There is a chemical necessity, as I have said, that makes dreaming inevitable. But then these dreams in turn affect the personality in general, and affect the actions of that personality in a physical universe. It goes without saying that telepathy operates within the dreaming state quite as effectively as it operates while the individual is awake. In the waking state it operates subconsciously. But in all times there is no boundary, generally speaking, that exists to separate one psychological unit from another. There are differences between psychological units, and you concentrate upon these differences. Nevertheless one man’s dreams affect another’s, and that man is in turn affected by the dreams of his neighbor.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第193节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "193", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0118", "zh": "举例来说，做梦者A或许会以心电感应方式，捕捉到做梦者B梦境中一小部分但很特别的内容。做梦者A不一定跟做梦者B有情感连结，然而，最起码他跟做梦者B的梦中事件会有情感连结，因为这个事件对做梦者A有重大意义。或许某甲梦到小时候被狗咬的经验，另一个也被狗咬过的某乙，可能会以心电感应的方式捕捉到那个梦。并不是因为某乙跟这个做梦者某甲有关，而是因为这个经验会冲击到他的情感，于是他就会吸引到这个梦。", "en": "Dreamer “A” for example may pick up telepathically a small but particular portion of a dream by dreamer “B”. Dreamer “A” need not necessarily have an emotional connection with dreamer “B”. However there will be at the very least an emotional connection between the event within dreamer “B’s” dream, that has strong meaning for dreamer “A”. A man may dream of a childhood experience in which he was bitten by a dog. Another man who was also bitten by a dog, may then for example telepathically pick up the original dream. Not because he is necessarily connected with the dreamer, but because the experience will strike at him emotionally, and he will then attract the dream.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第195节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "195", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0120", "zh": "我之前概略解释过做梦的人可能会以心电感应的方式，与另一人的梦沟通的方法，但不见得是因为他认识那个人，在很多状况下他们互不相识。两人间的心电感应之所以会出现，是由于吸引力，也就是第二个做梦者散发出个人情感电荷，让这些沟通管道得以开放。", "en": "Briefly, I explained the way in which a dreamer may be telepathically in communication with another man’s dream. Not necessarily because he is aware of the man, for in many cases he is not. The telepathic communication arises as a result of an attraction, a personal emotional charge on the part of the second dreamer that allows him to open these channels of communication.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第196节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "196", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0127", "zh": "当肉身的自己睡着的时候，星光的形象就真的开始游荡。当物质生命还在的时候，它总是会回归肉体。当自己睡着的时候，它的心电感应和预知能力并不会被自我以任何方式所阻碍。在醒着的时候，沟通系统或多或少在自我那方被关闭，但在睡眠时，屏障会打开，从内我来的知识会更自由的流动。", "en": "When the physical self sleeps the astral image may indeed wander. It always returns to the physical body during physical life. Its telepathic and clairvoyant abilities are not hampered in any way by the ego when that self sleeps. In waking hours the communications system is more or less closed on the ego’s side, but in sleep the barriers are lifted and knowledge from the inner self has a freer flow.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第202节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "202", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": "死后与出生前", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0158", "zh": "例如，死后犹存的人格主要依赖心电感应沟通。死后犹存的人格不是用语言来思考，而是以更为直接得多的方式体验概念。以身体为导向的个体根本无法了解这种事情。", "en": "The survival personality for example relies mainly upon telepathic communication. The survival personality does not think in terms of words, but experiences concepts in a much more direct manner. This sort of thing simply could not be understood by the physically-oriented individual.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第242节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "242", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0253", "zh": "你对也是已经死亡的亲人的真正感情瞒不了你也瞒不了他们。没有虚伪。你不会假装去爱一个没做了什么事来赢取你的敬爱的父亲或母亲。在这死后的期间里，心电感应无扭曲地运作，因此你必须处理存在于你自己与所有在等着你的亲友间的真正关系。", "en": "Your true feeling toward relatives who are also dead will be known to you and to them. There is no hypocrisy. You do not pretend to love a parent who did little to earn your respect or love. Telepathy operates without distortion in this after-death period, so you must deal with the true relationships that exist between yourself and all relatives and friends who await you.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第535节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "535", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0257", "zh": "在下一生的各种关系必须订定下来，而这涉及了和那些将牵涉在内的人作心电感应的沟通。那么，这是一个有许多投射的时期。有些人根本是独行侠，他对地球上的各个历史时期并没有任何强烈的感情就投胎了。还有些人喜欢和他们在过去某个特定历史时期同时代的人一同回来，所以有些集体的转生模式，在其中有许多人（但并非所有的人）——都一同地卷入于转世的周期里。", "en": "The relationships for the next life have to be settled upon, and this involves telepathic communication with all those who will be involved. This is a time, then, of many projections. There are those who are simply loners, who reincarnate without any great feeling for earth’s historical periods. There are others who like to return when their contemporaries from some particular past historical time return again, and therefore there are group patterns that involve reincarnational cycles in which many, but not all, are involved.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第541节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "541", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0242", "zh": "它听得见我的声音，但它是在心智上理解我所说的话。它已如此深入物质实相（苏已怀孕八个月），以致它能以心电感应来知觉，但如你们所知，还要过一段时间，它才能诠释语言本身。它将依赖内在的沟通。", "en": "It hears my voice, but it understands what I am saying mentally. It has come so far into physical reality (Sue is eight months pregnant), that it can perceive telepathically, but it will be some time, as you know, before it will be able to interpret speech as such. It will rely upon inner communication.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第499节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "499", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [{"id": "q-concept-069-e0004", "zh": "那么，你们为什么要坚持认为心电感应或预感这种内在经验就不存在，因为你们无法用以双手握住它。所以像心电感应或预感这种内在经验就不存在？在很多情况下，别人却可以用一种无法证实的纯粹心理经验方式，证实这种情形。And yet in many instances such cases can be corroborated by others in a manner in which a purely psychological experience cannot be corroborated.然而在许多情形中，这样的案例是可以经由他人证实的，而纯心理体验却无法以同样的方式被证实。", "en": "Why then do you insist that an inner experience such as telepathy or premonition does not exist because you cannot hold it in both hands? And yet in many instances such cases can be corroborated by others in a manner in which a purely psychological experience cannot be corroborated.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第26节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "26", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0007", "zh": "我想要让你们看到心灵感应确实存在，也想要让鲁柏看到，涉及的不只是他自己的潜意识。我想要建立他的信心。我绝对是独立在鲁柏潜意识之外的一个人格。现在，鲁柏把我组合起来，或说允许我组合我自己，用一种你们认得出我的方式；但不管这个组合怎样，我都是带着我说过的前世独立存在的。", "en": "I wanted to show you that telepathy did exist, and I wanted to show Ruburt that more than his own subconscious was involved. I wanted to build up his confidence. I am definitely a personality independent of Ruburt’s subconscious. Now, Ruburt assembles me, or allows me to assemble myself, in a way that will be recognizable to you; but regardless of this assembling, I exist in an independent manner, and with the past of which I have spoken.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第28节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "28", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0025", "zh": "个人永远会受到灾难的警告，这样有机体就能提前做好准备。死亡的日期是知晓的。意识上，基于明显可见的理由，这样的知识，不会给自我，但每个有机体，通过它的内在感官，具备个人灾难、死亡等潜意识知识，人格本身会事先决定它所认为的灾难；人类的成员整体而言都事先知道他们的战争。心灵感应持续在潜意识层运行，作为所有语言和沟通的基础，同样的，千里眼也在持续不断地运作，以使物质有机体可以做好准备去面对挑战。", "en": "Individuals are always warned of disasters, so that the organism can prepare itself ahead of time. The day of death is known. Consciously such knowledge is not given to the ego for obvious reasons, but every organism, through its inner senses, is equipped with subconscious knowledge of personal disasters, deaths, and so forth, the personality itself deciding beforehand what it considers disastrous; and the members of the species as a whole know in advance of their wars. As telepathy operates constantly at a subconscious level, as a basis for all language and communication, so clairvoyance operates continually so that the physical organism can prepare itself to face its challenges.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0026", "zh": "催眠将越来越是科学调查的一个工具。心灵感应将会被证实确有其事，并且被加以利用，但非常可悲的是，它一开始是为了达到战争和阴谋的目的。即便如此，心灵感应将使你们的种族，有能力与外星智慧（alien intelligence）进行第一次接触。一开始你们不会认出是这样。", "en": "Hypnotism will become more and more a tool of scientific investigation. Telepathy will be proven without a doubt, and utilized, sadly enough in the beginning, for purposes of war and intrigue. Nevertheless telepathy will enable your race to make its first contact with alien intelligence. It will not at first be recognized as such.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第45节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "45", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0041", "zh": "在任何层面上，任何处境下，意念永远源自于个体。无论如何，意念一旦产生，就被个体赋予能量实相，因此获得它们自己的一种生命力。透过心灵感应的沟通，意念被潜意识接收到。但它们不一定直接被一个心智接收，也就是说，不一定要有直接的沟通。", "en": "Ideas originate always from individuals on any plane, and under any circumstance. The ideas once originated, however, are given energy reality by the individual and therefore attain a vitality of their own. The ideas are picked up by the subconscious through a telepathic communication. They do not however have to be picked up directly from one mind, that is, there does not have to be direct communication.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第66节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "66", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0052", "zh": "后记：出于你们本身的心理内涵，你们往往会挡掉你们自己的内在资料，但你们会从另一个来源，例如一个朋友，透过心灵感应接受相同的基本资料。", "en": "Often, as a postscript, you will personally block inner data of your own because of your own psychological connotations, but you will accept the same basic material telepathically from another source, such as a friend.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第77节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "77", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0065", "zh": "你们各自有自己独特的进步方式，你，约瑟，会发现你接收心电感应资料的能力显露在心理时间实验以及梦中，也展现在一般意识期间自发的灵光乍现之中。", "en": "You have each your own characteristic ways of advancement. You will discover, Joseph, that your ability to receive so-called telepathic data is showing itself in psychological time experiments and dreams, as well as in spontaneous flashes during regular consciousness.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第104节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "104", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0109", "zh": "在良好的情境下，鲁伯会沉入这个能量池（energy pool）之中，显然那里面一定包含了参与者个人经验的某些元素。我之前就打算提供这些讯息给你们，而你们很快就会明白，为什么梦境中比较容易产生心电感应和千里眼的现象。", "en": "In good circumstances Ruburt then dips into this energy pool, which obviously must contain certain elements of personal experience on the part of the participators. I have meant to give you this information in the past, and shortly you will see why telepathy and clairvoyance occur more readily in the dream state.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第191节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "191", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0210", "zh": "任何两个或两个以上同住的人，都生活在一个由所有参与者形成的心灵环境里。的确，一个人在惯常生病的期间，会或多或少变得容易受负面的心灵环境因素影响。另一个人确实可以用心电感应帮助改变内在的气候——借由注入信心与力量的观念，从而把心灵气候改变到足够的程度，让抱病的人格随后能为自己多做些事。", "en": "Any two or more individuals living together, live in a psychic environment formed by all involved. It is true that one in a period of illness habitually, to one extent or another, becomes susceptible to negative psychic environmentals. The other can indeed telepathically help change the inner climate by inserting ideas of confidence and strength, and thus changing the psychic climate enough so that the ailing personality can then do more on their own behalf.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第437节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "437", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0216", "zh": "不过，如今在任何心电感应的实验里，只要时段安静，你就应当会有极好的表现，因为那块屏幕已不再需要，而你已把它大体抛开。同样的事在家庭生活中以无穷的变化发生着。有时，天生的心电感应能力能帮助养育孩子。还要记得，你也从父母那里收到过许多支持性的印象。", "en": "You should however do very well now in periods of quiet in any telepathic experiments, for the screen is no longer needed and you have largely discarded it. The same sort of events occur with infinite variations in family life. At times the natural telepathic abilities can help nurture the children. And remember that you also received many supportive impressions from your parents also.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第445节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "445", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0276", "zh": "我们一直在谈论“意识心”，因为它就是你在物质世界中一切活动的总指挥。我告诉过你（在本章之初）了解自我的重要性，自我是内我最“外在”的部分，并没有被疏离，而是往外看向物质实相。用这个比喻来说，居于意识心另一面的“我”的那部分，则不停地接收心电感应的资料。要记住，实际上亦没有分割，我这样说只是为了便于讨论而已。", "en": "Now we have been speaking of the conscious mind, for it is the director of your activities physically. I told you (at the beginning of this chapter) that it was important to realize the ego’s position as the most “exterior” portion of the inner self, not alienated but looking outward to physical reality. Using this analogy, portions of the self on the other side of the conscious mind constantly receive telepathic data. Remember, there are no divisions, so the terms used are simply to make the discussion easier.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0277", "zh": "用我们的比喻来说，心电感应式的讯息，来自“自己”更深的部分。这些部分的接受能力强得令人惊奇，以致必须要有某些组织来筛选过滤这些资料。有一些根本与你无关，它是关于你所不知的人的资料。", "en": "Now: The telepathic information, using our analogy, comes through deeper portions of the self. These parts have such an amazing capacity to receive that some organization is necessary to sift the data. Some is simply not important to you. It concerns people of whom you have no other knowledge.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-069-e0287", "zh": "这后面藏着的信念就是“任何伤害不可避免是灾难”。这样的一个信念，可以源自，比如说，一位过度操心的母亲。如果这样一个母亲的想象跟着她的信念走——势必如此——那么她就会立刻在一个最微不足道的威胁上，感知她的孩子身边有个潜在的大危险。在这种情形下，孩子透过母亲的行为，同时透过感知心电感应，接到这样一个讯息，而按照那些心照不宣的信念作出反应。", "en": "Behind this would be the belief that any hurt was inherently a disaster. Such a belief could originate from an overanxious mother, for instance. If such a mother’s imagination followed her belief — as of course it would — then she would immediately perceive a great potential danger to her child in the smallest threat. Both through the mother’s actions, and telepathically, the child would receive such a message and react according to those understood beliefs.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第619节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "619", "only_en": false}], "books": [{"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 13}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 9}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 7}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 2}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 2}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 1}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 1}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 9, "quotes": 74, "reading": 13, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 0}};
